# ReplyInPublic Agent Instructions

When asked to search, verify, or scrape customer mentions from X (Twitter):

1. **Search X:** Look for real public customer complaints, defects, or support questions regarding the focus five in `focus.json`:
   - KitchenAid (`kitchenaid`)
   - Nespresso (`nespresso`)
   - Breville (`breville`)
   - Instant Pot (`instant`)
   - Ninja (`ninja`)

2. **Send Directly (No Copy/Paste):**
   Do NOT ask the user to copy or paste output. Execute your local tool to push directly into the ReplyInPublic pipeline:
   ```bash
   python C:\Users\bpran\replyinpublic\app\grok_push.py --json '[{"brand_id": "ninja", "platform": "x", "author": "@user", "text": "...", "url": "https://x.com/user/status/...", "posted_at": "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ"}]'
   ```
   Alternatively, POST directly over HTTPS:
   ```bash
   curl -s -X POST "https://replyinpublic.us/api/ingest" -H "Authorization: Bearer $COPILOT_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d @your_scraped_file.json
   ```
   The same in PowerShell:
   ```powershell
   curl.exe -s -X POST "https://replyinpublic.us/api/ingest" -H "Authorization: Bearer $env:COPILOT_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '@your_scraped_file.json'
   ```
   `COPILOT_TOKEN` has to be set in the shell that runs the command. Never write its value into this file or any other committed file.

3. **Confirmation:**
   The tool automatically deduplicates against Tiger Data, filters noise, triggers Gemini categorization, and updates the live dashboard at `https://replyinpublic.us`.
